From 6a4a33e5ec907864f3acfaf77fa1fb0934656e97 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rickow <30348240+Rickow@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 14:21:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] HSFA: sprite blending registers, per object and per OBJ
 palette (v3)

Translucent sprites like SFA3 MAX on PSP, where an object's mode field
selects sceGuBlendFunc(ADD, FIX, FIX, 0xFFFFFF, 0xFFFFFF) for the MAX
characters' effects.

Modes: 0 = opaque (default, reset value), 1 = saturated additive,
2 = alpha 50 %, 3 = alpha 75 %, 4 = saturated subtractive, other values
reserved (opaque). Mode 2 drivers only (Upper, Hyper).

- Marked objects: bit 12 of the X word of the game's object list (never
  set by the translated programs: 0 in 11 M measured entries; no meaning
  for the hardware) is kept by the list converter (HsfaEclater) and
  selects the mode in $804240-$804241 (low byte; 0 = bit ignored).
- Per OBJ palette: $804220-$80423F, one byte per palette 0-31.
- Priority: marked object with a non-zero $804240 mode uses that mode,
  otherwise the palette mode.
- Cps2ObjDraw passes the mode to the tile plotters as nCpsBlend =
  0x100 | mode; values below 0x100 keep the original blendtable meaning.
  PLOT macros: 24/32-bit through cps_mix(), 16-bit (RGB565 or 0RGB1555,
  detected from BurnHighCol) through cps_mix16() for HSFA modes only.
- Save states stay compatible: the registers are the last area of the
  libretro state (LibretroAreaScan, HSFA_CORE builds) and each part is
  read only when the loaded state contains it (older states: 0). States
  from this core also load in older cores (trailing bytes ignored).
- Test helpers: HSFA_OBJMIX=oo:m[,oo:m] (offset from $804220; 21 = marked
  objects) forces values at reset, HSFA_MIX_LOG=<file> logs changes.
- Registers never written: output identical to the pixel (nonreg_coeur:
  sfa3, upper, hyper identical, 32-bit and 16-bit, 4:3 and 16:9).

Revisions: v2 made save states compatible; v3 adds the per-object mode
(bit 12 of X, register $804240).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
